  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project in Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to improve protection, access to justice, and social inclusion for LGBTQIA+ people in Nigeria, who continue to face violence, discrimination, and exclusion from families, communities, religious institutions, and state actors. Many survivors experience abuse within the family, including forced marriage, conversion practices, extortion, and physical or psychological violence, while weak redress systems allow impunity to persist.

The Margins to Mainstream programme adopts a regionally tailored approach across Nigeria&#x2019;s six geopolitical zones. It will recruit six regional responders to coordinate case documentation, referrals, and survivor support through partner networks. The project will engage the Nigeria Police Force and National Human Rights Commission to improve accountability and institutional responses to violations. Public education, family sensitisation, and faith-based dialogues will challenge harmful narratives, reduce stigma, and promote safer, more inclusive communities for LGBTQIA+ people.</narrative>
  </description>
